{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "av1-obu-reading",
  "gate": "required",
  "operation": "av1-obu-reading",
  "candidate": "framing-views-worker",
  "worker_operation": "obu-",
  "runner": "cargo xtask report",
  "reference": "ffmpeg-framing-views-native",
  "contract": [
    "Read every temporal unit in its AV1 IVF envelope. The candidate drives the incremental OBU reader at the stated window size. The reference submits the complete temporal unit to filter_units with an excluded type absent from the unit, then reads the public wire syntax of its output. If the filter refuses a low-overhead temporal unit truncated after complete OBUs, submit the complete prefix separately and compare every returned OBU before the refusal. The filter may inspect OBU contents.",
    "Fold kind 1 with temporal unit index, OBU type, extension presence, temporal and spatial IDs (zero when absent), size presence, payload length and every payload byte. Fold kind 7 with the temporal unit index and OBU count on clean end or kind 8 with the index on refusal. An empty low-overhead unit carries zero OBUs.",
    "IVF envelope loading and parsing are outside the operation. Reader or filter construction, all units and teardown are inside."
  ],
  "required_profiles": [
    "authored-low-overhead",
    "authored-single",
    "encoded-authored",
    "fate"
  ],
  "required_targets": [
    "aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu",
    "thumbv7neon-unknown-linux-gnueabihf"
  ],
  "iterations": 50,
  "minimum_pairs": 30,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "pending_module_requirements": [
    "The AV1 framing reader exposes the three wire units; the filter also interprets their payload syntax and refuses this opaque sequence header. A like-for-like reference operation needs to expose units before payload interpretation."
  ],
  "open_cases": [
    {
      "id": "three-obu-order-w1",
      "requirement": "The AV1 framing reader exposes the three wire units; the filter also interprets their payload syntax and refuses this opaque sequence header. A like-for-like reference operation needs to expose units before payload interpretation."
    }
  ],
  "open_deviations": [
    {
      "reading": "Read nonzero forbidden or reserved bits as source diagnostics",
      "clause": "AV1 Bitstream v1.0.0 with Errata 1 clauses 5.3.2–5.3.3 and 6.2.2–6.2.3 (header and extension zero bits)",
      "candidate": "retains the complete OBU and reports the offending bits in the wire view",
      "reference": "refuses the packet",
      "cases": [
        "extension-1-w1",
        "extension-7-w1",
        "extension-255-w1",
        "zero-bit-issues-1-0-w1",
        "zero-bit-issues-0-1-w1",
        "zero-bit-issues-1-1-w1",
        "external-unsized-extension-255-w1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "reading": "Low-overhead OBUs carry their own size field",
      "clause": "AV1 Bitstream v1.0.0 with Errata 1 clause 5.2 (obu_has_size_field shall equal 1)",
      "candidate": "refuses the size-less unit in low-overhead mode",
      "reference": "uses its packet boundary as the extent and emits the size-less unit",
      "compat": "Av1ObuFraming::OneObu when the caller supplies that extent",
      "cases": [
        "low-unsized-w1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "reading": "A caller's OBU count bound",
      "clause": "AV1 Bitstream v1.0.0 with Errata 1 clause 5.2 (series of OBUs) and Av1ObuLimits::maximum_obus",
      "candidate": "returns the first 64 delimiters then refuses the 65th",
      "reference": "emits all 65 delimiters",
      "cases": [
        "obu-count-limit-w1"
      ]
    }
  ],
